id:                     E373
trigger_tool: conan|meson|python|buildbot
phase: build|testing|verification
error_signature: FileNotFoundError: \[Errno 2\] No such file or directory: 'meson'|self.run.*meson.*succeeds.*subprocess.run.*meson.*fails
severity: 2
category:               conan, environment
match_keywords: ConanFile.run, conanbuild, build scope, Meson introspection, subprocess.run, PATH, StringIO, Buildbot
title: Route build-tool introspection through the Conan build environment
root_cause: Conan applies generated conanbuild environment files around ConanFile.run in build scope, while a direct Python subprocess inherits the recipe process environment and can lose profile-provided build-tool PATH entries.
affected_scope: Conan 2 recipes that use profile-provided build tools for normal commands through self.run but invoke the same tools directly for JSON or metadata introspection.
verification_cmd: Run the production introspection helper with an empty host PATH, require explicit env=conanbuild and scope=build, then exercise nonzero, invalid-JSON, inventory-drift, missing-target, duplicate-ID, and selector-collision negatives.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: conan-self-run-captured-introspection
rec_description: Format the argv safely, execute through ConanFile.run in the conanbuild build scope with StringIO capture, reject nonzero status, and parse and validate the captured JSON fail-closed.
rec_command: self.run(formatted_command, stdout=stdout, stderr=stderr, ignore_errors=True, env="conanbuild", scope="build")
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: repair-build-tool-declaration-or-worker-profile
fallback_description: If the build environment itself cannot resolve the tool, repair the declared tool requirement or worker profile instead of hard-coding a transient worker path.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: subprocess\.run\(\["meson"|/storage/Users/.*/meson|ignore_errors=True.*return_code.*unchecked
forbid_1_reason: Bare subprocesses bypass generated Conan build environments, worker-specific absolute paths drift, and unchecked ignore_errors converts real introspection failures into misleading parser errors.
forbid_1_consequence: A recipe can compile successfully and then fail or misreport its upstream test inventory on a worker with a minimal process PATH.
doc_file: doc/E373.md
last_updated: 2026-08-17
source_event: pkgconf 3.0.5 PR #5532 Buildbot #26332 buildid 29163
authors: 2301_80739235 <2047361658@qq.com>
